---
title: "Pharmacology for Practical Nurses"
code: "PNE-173"
category: "practical-nursing"
credits: "2"
prerequisites: []
corequisites: []
---

Studies history, classification, sources, effects, uses and legalities of drugs. Teaches problem solving skills used in medication administrations. Emphasizes major drug classes and specific agents within each class. Lecture 2 hours per week. Additional course fee applies.
